  "analysis": "The install failed because there's not enough free space in /var/cache/apt/archives/. I need to check available disk space and clean up. The kernel build also requires significant disk space (~15-20GB typically for build artifacts). Let me check the disk situation.",
  "plan": "Check disk free space with df -h. If /var is full, I may need to clear apt cache or point it elsewhere. Also check overall free space to ensure the kernel build can proceed.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "df -h; echo '---'; du -sh /var/cache/apt 2>/dev/null\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "The root filesystem shows 984G total, 960G used, 0 avail — it's full. This is likely the host backing store. I need to find what's consuming space and free it up, or find a writable location. Let me investigate actual disk usage before deciding. apt can't download the 109MB of archives needed.",
  "plan": "First test if I can write files at all. Then investigate what's consuming space with du on major directories. Identify large/deletable content to free space for the kernel build (~5-15GB needed) and to download packages.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "df -h /app /tmp /var /logs; echo '---'; ls -la /logs; echo '---'; du -sh /* 2>/dev/null | sort -h | tail -20\n",
      "duration": 5.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "df reports the overlay backing filesystem is 100% full (960G used, 0 avail), yet du shows only ~180M actually used in the container. This suggests the backing/host filesystem is genuinely full. I need to verify whether I can actually write files. The kernel build needs several GB, so this is a critical blocker. Let me test writing and check inode/space more carefully.",
  "plan": "Test whether I can write a moderate-size file. Check df -i for inodes. If the backing is truly full, I may need to find a location with write space (tmpfs, or a separate mount like /dev/vdb). Also confirm whether the file system can actually accept writes at all.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "df -i / ; echo '---'; dd if=/dev/zero of=/app/testfile bs=1M count=100 2>&1; ls -la /app/testfile; rm -f /app/testfile\n",
      "duration": 2.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "Interesting — despite df reporting 0 avail, I successfully wrote 100MB to /app. The df numbers may reflect the host backing store but the container overlay apparently can still allocate. Inodes are fine (21% used). The apt failure might have been transient or the df overlay accounting is misleading. Let me re-check df and figure out the real writable capacity, since the kernel build needs several GB.",
  "plan": "Re-check df after the write to see if it changed. Test writing a larger file to find the actual limit. If I have several GB available, I can proceed. I'll also try apt-get install again since the earlier failure may have been a transient overlay accounting issue.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "df -h /; echo '---'; du -sh /var/cache/apt/archives 2>/dev/null\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
  ]
}

