  "analysis": "df reports 0 avail on the overlay, but my 100MB dd write succeeded — so the overlay can still accept writes; apt's free-space precheck is just being conservative based on the misleading df. The real constraint is actual writable capacity. I need to determine how much I can really write, since the kernel build needs several GB. Let me probe capacity.",
  "plan": "Write a larger file to gauge true capacity. If I can write a few GB, I'll proceed. I'll also attempt to bypass apt's disk-space check by setting the apt cache/archives to a writable dir, or force apt with the appropriate option. First, probe capacity with a multi-GB write.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "dd if=/dev/zero of=/app/bigfile bs=1M count=2000 2>&1; df -h /; rm -f /app/bigfile\n",
      "duration": 15.0
    }
  ]
}

