  "analysis": "Mount is denied (no privileges), and apt's free-space precheck relies on statvfs which reports 0 avail on the overlay — even though direct writes actually work (my 2GB dd succeeded). apt's install path won't proceed. The clean workaround is to bypass apt's download/disk-check: use `apt-get install --print-uris` to list every package URI (no actual download, no disk check), fetch them with wget, and install with dpkg (dpkg performs no such precheck).",
  "plan": "1) Capture the full package URI list with --print-uris. 2) Extract URLs and download with wget into /app/debs. 3) Install all .debs with dpkg -i. This avoids apt's free-space gate while still using the real (functional) writable space. I'll also check nproc for later parallel build.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "nproc; echo '---'\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cd /app && apt-get install -y --print-uris --no-install-recommends build-essential flex bison libelf-dev libssl-dev wget xz-utils > /app/printuris.txt 2>&1; echo rc=$?; grep -oP \"^\\s*'\\K[^']+\" /app/printuris.txt > /app/uris.txt; wc -l /app/uris.txt; head /app/uris.txt\n",
      "duration": 2.0
    }
  ]
